  "worked_solution": "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202x} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}, \\\\ \\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202y} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})^{2}+(\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+1}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\u222c}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (1-0)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
